VERSION 1.2
CONTEXT: "GEP-7 contract acceptance validation"
TARGET: "Python3"
TRACE: "GEP-7", "AT-GEP7-001", "AT-GEP7-002", "AT-GEP7-003", "AT-GEP7-004"

FLOW test_typed_contract_signatures():
    @trace(#AT-GEP7-001) AS AT_GEP7_TYPED_SIGNATURES
    1. ACHIEVE "Build a GASD 1.2 component with submit(items: List<Common.OrderItem>, limit: Integer) -> Result<Void> and reset() -> Void":
        POSTCONDITION: "Common is an import alias resolving OrderItem. Both contracts match their methods. The submit contract declares both inputs and the reset contract omits INPUT. Each has one outcome case."
    2. ACHIEVE "Run the validator and inspect the two contract ASTs":
        POSTCONDITION: "Validation passes. The AST preserves the input names, their order, the full qualified generic type, and the Result<Void> output. The reset contract has zero inputs."

FLOW test_ordered_contract_guards():
    @trace(#AT-GEP7-002) AS AT_GEP7_GUARD_ORDER
    1. ACHIEVE "Export a GASD 1.2 contract with input request bound to an OrderRequest type declaring quantity as Integer":
        POSTCONDITION: "Its guarded case starts with request != null, then request.quantity > 0. The contract also has an unguarded case. Both cases specify outcomes."
    2. ACHIEVE "Compare the contract cases in the syntactic and semantic AST exports":
        POSTCONDITION: "Both exports contain the same two guards, their operators and operands in source order, and an empty when array for the unguarded case."
    3. ACHIEVE "Evaluate the same cases against null, a positive quantity, and zero":
        POSTCONDITION: "Null short-circuits the field access. Positive quantity makes both cases eligible. Zero makes only the unguarded case eligible."

FLOW test_overlapping_payment_cases():
    @trace(#AT-GEP7-003) AS AT_GEP7_PAYMENT_CASES
    1. ACHIEVE "Build the payment contract with success, service_failure, timeout, and null_input cases":
        POSTCONDITION: "The first three guard on non-null email. Success requires ACTIVE status and a UUID customerId. Service failure requires PaymentGatewayException and two additional attempts. Timeout requires the same exception and at least 3000ms. The null_input case guards on null and requires IllegalArgumentException."
    2. ACHIEVE "Check null email before argument validation and check the resulting IllegalArgumentException":
        POSTCONDITION: "Only null_input is eligible and the exception verifies. A normal return for the same input violates the contract."
    3. ACHIEVE "Check three non-null observations with distinct matching requirements":
        POSTCONDITION: "An ACTIVE customer with a valid UUID verifies success. PaymentGatewayException with two additional attempts and less than 3000ms verifies service_failure. The same exception at 3000ms with zero retries verifies timeout."
    4. ACHIEVE "Repeat the observations with reversed case declarations":
        POSTCONDITION: "Each verification status and set of matching case names is unchanged."

FLOW test_quoted_postcondition_evidence():
    @trace(#AT-GEP7-004) AS AT_GEP7_QUOTED_EVIDENCE
    1. ACHIEVE "Verify a normal return against an eligible case with a formal predicate and a quoted postcondition":
        POSTCONDITION: "A true formal predicate with missing quoted evidence is unverified. Evidence confirming the quoted condition verifies the call. Evidence disproving it yields a violation."
    2. ACHIEVE "Check an observed return that fails the formal predicate and supply no quoted evidence":
        POSTCONDITION: "The call violates the contract because the case cannot match."
    3. ACHIEVE "Check a call with no eligible cases and a call with both a verified and an unverified case":
        POSTCONDITION: "The first call violates the contract. The second is verified regardless of case declaration order."
